WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820 line:88%
The historical timeline is a story of changing opportunity

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:04.700 line:88%
and control.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.930 line:88%
Deaf people worked as farmers, painters, and craftspeople.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.990 line:88%
Some served in the Ottoman Court, where signed communication

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.470 line:88%
and secrecy were useful.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.370 line:88%
Elsewhere, the belief that deaf people lacked reason was

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.710 line:88%
used to deny education and legal rights.

00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:23.821 line:88%
By the fifteen hundreds, educators recognized that deaf people

00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:24.701 line:88%
could be educated.

00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:28.201 line:88%
Some American families later sent children to European schools.

00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:31.451 line:88%
In eighteen seventeen, the school now called the American

00:00:31.451 --> 00:00:33.191 line:88%
School for the Deaf opened in Connecticut.

00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:36.521 line:88%
The late eighteen hundreds brought pressure to replace signing

00:00:36.521 --> 00:00:37.401 line:88%
with spoken English.

00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:40.559 line:88%
Two events share the year eighteen eighty.

00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:43.659 line:88%
The Milan Congress endorsed speech over sign language, with

00:00:43.659 --> 00:00:46.839 line:88%
just one deaf participant among one hundred sixty-four people.

00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:50.389 line:88%
The National Association of the Deaf was also founded

00:00:50.389 --> 00:00:51.089 line:88%
that year.

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:54.539 line:88%
Milan illustrates decisions dominated by hearing people.

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:58.839 line:88%
The association illustrates Deaf-led advocacy against discrimination.

00:00:59.673 --> 00:01:03.113 line:88%
In nineteen eighty-eight, Gallaudet University selected a hearing president.

00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:06.853 line:88%
The Deaf President Now protest challenged that choice and

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:08.973 line:88%
succeeded in securing a Deaf president.

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:13.283 line:88%
Connect these events through representation: who participates in decisions

00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:16.243 line:88%
about education, language, and institutional leadership?
